      en: "Lavumisa Freight Terminal on the South Africa border in southern Eswatini is a key transshipment point for cargo traffic. Expanded in the 2000s, it features container storage yards, cold storage facilities, and customs clearance. The terminal handles about 200,000 tonnes of freight annually, mainly agricultural products such as sugar, citrus, and vegetables. It employs around 150 people. Lavumisa is part of the trade route connecting Eswatini to the Port of Durban. The facility is critical to the country's export industry and has been upgraded with African Development Bank funding.",
